  "agreementAccept": "Accept and continue",
  "agreementMessage": "About the app\nDITING is an open-source tool focused on local DNS resolution optimisation and network rule filtering. It offers three work modes: normal, simple and server. Normal mode takes over all traffic through a full tunnel, simple mode takes over DNS queries only and lets other traffic go direct, while server mode serves DNS to the LAN. Everything runs locally on the device: no remote data upload and no privacy tracking.\n\nHow it works\nNormal and simple modes use the Android local VPN interface (simple mode can also use root takeover) and never connect to a remote VPN server. Each mode keeps its own rules, cache and logs; simple mode offers DNS filtering only and shows fewer categories in its feature hub by default, which can be restored at any time. Rules and logs stay on the device. Please understand the impact before enabling advanced extensions.\n\nDisclaimer\nThis software is provided as is. Users must comply with applicable laws and verify the legality and safety of the rules and upstream resolvers they configure. Any illegal use is strictly forbidden, and users bear all consequences of their own configuration or use of this software.",
